# echo problem
# Read all input and output exactly the same
# Stop when input is 0 (EOF)

# The issue: We need to NOT output when A is 0
# Strategy: Only output non-zero characters

# Initialize: mem[0] = 1 for halt condition
[0]<1

# Read character into A
A<I

# We need to halt if A is 0 BEFORE outputting
# Check halt condition first
Z<[A]
# If A=0, Z becomes 1 from mem[0], halts immediately
# If A!=0, Z becomes 0 from mem[A], continues

# Output A
O<A

# The code loops back to read next character
